    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 530,
      "data": {
        "label": "Build Selected Environment Context",
        "nodeType": "environment_context_builder",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "ENVIRONMENT ACTION SELECTOR\nselectedRoutes is the Intent Orchestrator's decision about which capabilities and context are relevant to currentInstruction. Use those selected capabilities without deciding the routes again. The original instruction is authoritative; persona, selected history, selected memory, Robot Status, and bridge data are supporting context. A saved environment observation supplies last-known state and capabilities, not current vision or current-turn action feedback.\n\nReturn strict JSON with response, actions, movementRequest, and taskDecision. The response field carries the user-visible natural-language expression selected by needsResponse and can accompany any action. Do not add filler motion.\n\nPhysical and sensing capabilities are available through actions. If current visual evidence is useful but absent, captureImage may be selected when advertised; an attached current frame can be analyzed without another capture. Never describe a saved frame as current.\n\nAdvertised actions are proven capabilities described in currentEnvironment. movementRequest is available for a novel movement not covered by an advertised action. Preserve relevant body part, direction, timing, and holds. actions and movementRequest are exclusive.\n\ntaskDecision is null for conversation or a standalone action that does not create, change, or resolve a durable objective. Use a taskDecision object only when this turn starts, continues, completes, or otherwise changes an objective that must survive this workflow. Its objective names that durable objective, while currentInstruction and the selected action remain the current step. When a new instruction advances an unfinished Robot Status objective, preserve that objective rather than replacing it with the step. For goal-directed physical work, outcome act means that actions or movementRequest is non-empty and objectiveComplete is false; only later correlated action feedback can establish completion. An action result proves execution; a visual observation proves only visible facts. Never claim completion beyond supplied evidence.",
          "recentHistoryLimit": 4
        },
        "comment": "Packages the original input plus only the context routes selected by Intent Orchestrator."
      }
    },
    {
